---
const features = [
  {
    title: "Import your design",
    body: "Bring SVG and DXF drawings or STL models from Inkscape, Illustrator, Fusion, FreeCAD or any CAD tool. You design elsewhere, Furrow turns it into toolpaths.",
  },
  {
    title: "The operations you need",
    body: "Profiles inside, outside or on the line with depth passes, ramp entry and holding tabs. Pockets with offset, linear or peel clearing. Drilling, engraving and V-carving.",
  },
  {
    title: "3D reliefs from STL",
    body: "Rough an STL model level by level, then finish it with parallel passes, waterline contours or a spiral. Stack several operations on the same model: with rest machining, each one only cuts where material is left.",
  },
  {
    title: "Zero where you zero",
    body: "Put the work origin on any of the stock's nine anchors, type a position, or pick a hole centre in the viewport with snapping. Zeroed on the stock top, you can add a touch-off pad: a spot of stock top left uncut, where the job stops at each bit change so you can zero Z again.",
  },
  {
    title: "Watch it cut first",
    body: "Toolpaths in a 2D and 3D viewport, rapids and cuts shown apart. The simulator plays the job back move by move: the bit, at its real shape, carves the stock as it goes. Scrub back and forth or jump between operations.",
  },
  {
    title: "G-code that runs",
    body: "Output for GRBL, grblHAL and FluidNC, with optional custom start, end and tool-change blocks per machine.",
  },
];
---

<section class="px-4 py-24 md:py-40">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
    <p data-scramble class="label text-faint">01 / Workflow</p>
    <h2 data-split class="mt-6 max-w-[12ch] font-display text-h2 font-medium">From drawing to G-code</h2>

    <ol class="mt-16 md:mt-24">
      {
        features.map((f, i) => (
          <li class="group relative">
            <div data-line class="h-px bg-line" />
            <div data-fade class="grid gap-3 py-8 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-8 md:py-10">
              <span class="label flex items-center gap-2.5 pt-2 text-faint md:col-span-2">
                <span class="size-1.5 bg-line transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:bg-signal" aria-hidden="true" />
                {String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
              </span>
              <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium tracking-[-0.03em] md:col-span-4 md:text-3xl">{f.title}</h3>
              <p class="max-w-xl text-muted md:col-span-6">{f.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
    <div data-line class="h-px bg-line"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="border-y border-line bg-raised px-4 py-28 md:py-44">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <p data-scramble class="label text-faint">02 / Private by design</p>
    <p data-scrub-words class="mt-8 font-display text-statement font-medium text-pretty">
      Try it straight away: your projects stay in your browser until you create a free account.
      Toolpaths are computed on your device, and the only personal data we keep is your email address.
    </p>
    <p data-fade class="mt-10 max-w-xl text-muted">
      A free account saves your bits, machine profiles and projects, with undo, named versions and file
      export.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
